* **D2 (`M_power` unkilled by construction) — `UPHOLD`** (`READ` / `REASONED` / `MEASURED`): Because no caller in `GXEMUL-SEC/src` ever invokes `sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_RESET_POWER, ...)` (`0x000`), adding `|| expevt == EXPEVT_RESET_POWER` to `if (expevt != EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT)` is a dead branch on all reachable executions (`10/10` in [M_power.raw](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/M_power.raw)); no guest-reachable test can kill `M_power` without fabricating a synthetic caller, so disclosing it as an equivalent mutant on reachable states in [PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out#L85-L94) is the right engineering disposition.

---

### 2. Which Accepted Disposition Is Most Likely Wrong and Why? (Section 6, Question 2)

**`P8` (together with the identical `mtime` order-proof clause in `P1`) is the accepted disposition that contains a demonstrably false factual claim** (`READ` / `MEASURED` / `REASONED`):

1. **Why `P8` (and `P1`)'s `mtime` order proof is self-refuting**:
