   - Both claims are **structurally impossible on a POSIX/NTFS filesystem once the post-leg result is recorded in the same file**: because [PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out#L28-L32) and [`:111-116`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out#L111-L116) were edited in-place *after* `M_guard` (`19:14:12`) and `M_resinst` (`19:24:09`) finished in order to append the `MEASURED (MGUARD.log, M_guard.raw):` and `MEASURED (MUTLEG_M_resinst.log, M_resinst.raw):` paragraphs, each post-leg save overwrote `PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out`'s single filesystem `mtime` to a **post-leg** timestamp (`19:14:37` after `M_guard`, `19:24:29` after `M_resinst`, and currently `20:12:28` on disk). Indeed, [PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/PRETABLE_CORRECTION.out#L34-L41) itself now carries an in-file `NOTE ON MTIMES` acknowledging this exact trap.
