### 3. What Did All of Us Miss? (Section 6, Question 3)

1. **The `SR.RB` Guard-Narrowing Escape (The Primary Real-World `BL=1` Hardware State Is `RB=1`, Yet All 3 `BL=1` Probe Rows Use `RB=0`)** (`READ` / `REASONED`):
   - In `P1`, the panel tested *widening* the guard (`cpu->cd.sh.sr & (SH_SR_BL | SH_SR_MD)`), which `tlbm trapa` (`BL=0, MD=1`) killed, and noted in [sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py#L221-L223) that qualifying the guard with `SR.IMASK == 0xf` (and in [regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L221-L225), `SR.MD == 1`) is not caught because all three `BL=1` rows use `SR_MD_BL = 0x500000f0`.
   - What everyone missed is **`SH_SR_RB` (`0x20000000`, Register Bank bit)** (as well as `SH_SR_FD` `0x00008000`):
     - When a real SuperH guest enters an exception or interrupt handler, [`sh_exception`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L961) sets:
       `cpu->cd.sh.sr |= (SH_SR_MD | SH_SR_RB | SH_SR_BL);` (`0x700000f0`).
     - Therefore, in real guest software, an unexpected synchronous general exception while `SR.BL == 1` (the exact scenario `#577` exists to fix!) almost always happens inside an exception handler while **`SR.RB == 1`** (`sr = 0x700000x0`), **not** `SR.RB == 0` (`sr = 0x500000f0`).
     - Because all three `BL=1` rows in [sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py#L31-L32) and [`:193-199`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py#L193-L199) preset `SR_MD_BL = 0x500000f0` (`MD=1, RB=0, BL=1, FD=0, IMASK=0xf`), a mutant that narrows the guard to `RB == 0` — e.g., `if ((cpu->cd.sh.sr & (SH_SR_BL | SH_SR_RB)) == SH_SR_BL)` — passes **all 10 rows (`10/10`)** while completely breaking `#577` for every real-world exception handler running with `SR = 0x700000f0` (`MD|RB|BL`)!

2. **Pre-`sh_exception` Architectural Side Effects on `BL=1` General Exceptions (`cpu->cd.sh.tra` Written Before `sh_exception` in `X(trapa)`)** (`READ` / `REASONED`):
   - In [`X(trapa)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh_instr.c#L2857-L2858):
     ```c
     cpu->cd.sh.tra = ic->arg[0];
     sh_exception(cpu, EXPEVT_TRAPA, 0, 0);
     ```
   - When `TRAPA #imm` executes with `SR.BL = 1`, `cpu->cd.sh.tra` is unconditionally written *before* `sh_exception()` rewrites `EXPEVT_TRAPA` to `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` (`0x020`).
   - By contrast, for `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS_LD/ST` and `EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD/ST`, `TEA` (`SH4_MMU_TEA`) and `PTEH` (`SH4_MMU_PTEH`) are updated inside [`sh_exception`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L1032-L1093) *after* `switch (expevt)`, so rewriting `expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` at `:925` skips the `TEA`/`PTEH` update and jumps to `case EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL:` (`:1025`).
   - Why this is benign for `#577` (`REASONED`): [sh7750_hardware.txt](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/sh7750_hardware.txt) Table 5.1 (`:11977`) and `Manual_reset()` (`:12391-12404`) leave `TRA`, `TEA`, `SPC`, and `SSR` undefined (`Held`/`—`) on Manual Reset (`H'020`), so clobbering `tra` in `X(trapa)` while leaving `TEA`/`PTEH` untouched in `sh_exception()` does not violate the SH7750 manual. However, nobody on the panel noticed the asymmetry between `TRA` (written in caller before `sh_exception`) and `TEA`/`PTEH` (written in `switch (expevt)` after the `BL=1` rewrite).

3. **Contradiction Between the Brief's Clean-Tree Premise and the On-Disk Working Tree** (`READ` / `MEASURED`):
   - [brief_shblreset_f2.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w577/brief_shblreset_f2.md#L13) states:
     > *"THE TREE UNDER REVIEW IS `GXEMUL-SEC/src/` at HEAD; the diff is applied only in the scratch clone `/tmp/gxfix577`. No project tree is edited."*
   - In reality, on disk in `C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\GXEMUL-SEC`, the `#577` changes **are already applied in the working tree** ([cpu_sh.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c#L910-L927), [sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L180-L241), and [OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md#L24092-L24115)), and as noted under `P6`, [regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/sh_tlbmulti_probe.py#L221-L225) was edited *after* [sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/sh_tlbmulti_probe.NEW.py) and [ASRUN_NOTE.txt](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/shblreset/killtable_20261102/ASRUN_NOTE.txt) were frozen.

